From 7b3a06a5e93772ef03e13a40509be950dd5098b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:38:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] fix-data-6: P-3 full-time hourly pay at its posted
 rate; C-1 equally similar comparables spread across the estimate's pay

P-3 (public/app.js): a full-time posting paid by the hour leads with its posted
rate on the card ('$31.39-54.90/hour'; whole dollars at 340 px and under) and
the job page ('... an hour', 'USD - paid by the hour'), with the yearly figure
in the tip and an 'About $65K-114K a year (2,080 hours)' line, converted.
Sorting, the pay filter and the chart keep the yearly figure. Pay by place rows
too. Not shift pay, internships' terms or part-time pay (unchanged).

C-1 (public/features/compstimate.js shownComparables): where more roles are
equally similar than the five listed, the list shows ones nearest the estimate's
middle, low and high ends and halfway between, lowest pay first. The estimate is
worked out from every comparable as before.

e2e: P-3 and C-1 tests; P-1's job opener accepts the readable title.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
